<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><BaseHead title="Suzanne | 2007 Suzuki RM125 Frame-Up Rebuild | Marc Sherwood" description="Meet Suzanne, a 2007 Suzuki RM125 brought back through a frame-up rebuild. Before-and-after photos and the story of this yellow two-stroke motocross bike."/><meta name="theme-color" content="#101b1d"/>
<style>
html{scroll-behavior:smooth}body{margin:0;background:#101b1d;color:#f5f4ee;font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',sans-serif}*{box-sizing:border-box}a{color:inherit}.wrap{max-width:1120px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 24px}.top{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;padding:24px 0}.brand{font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;letter-spacing:-.03em}.brand b,.eyebrow{color:#d8f16a}.nav{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:18px;font-size:14px}.nav a{text-decoration:none;color:#c8d6cf}.hero{min-height:580px;display:flex;align-items:center;position:relative;overflow:hidden;background:#1a3030}.hero>img{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;object-position:center 38%}.hero:after{content:'';position:absolute;inset:0;background:linear-gradient(90deg,#101b1df8 0%,#101b1dd9 43%,#101b1d45 100%)}.hero .wrap{position:relative;z-index:1;width:100%;padding-top:100px;padding-bottom:105px}.eyebrow{font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.16em;font-size:12px}.hero h1{font-size:clamp(66px,12vw,148px);letter-spacing:-.085em;line-height:.9;margin:20px 0 24px}.hero p{font-size:clamp(19px,2.4vw,27px);line-height:1.5;max-width:560px;color:#dfe8e2}.btn{display:inline-block;background:#d8f16a;color:#13221b!important;text-decoration:none;font-weight:800;padding:16px 23px;margin-top:22px}.section{padding:80px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #354c47}.section.alt{background:#162629}.section h2{font-size:clamp(39px,5vw,62px);letter-spacing:-.06em;line-height:1.06;margin:14px 0 25px}.copy{font-size:18px;line-height:1.85;max-width:820px;color:#d1ddd6}.gallery{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:18px;margin-top:30px}.gallery a{display:block;background:#243638;text-decoration:none;overflow:hidden}.gallery img{display:block;width:100%;aspect-ratio:4/3;object-fit:cover}.gallery span{display:block;padding:16px;color:#d9e6df;font-weight:700;font-size:14px}.gallery a:first-child{grid-column:span 2}.gallery a:first-child img{aspect-ratio:16/9;object-fit:contain;background:#283638}.contact{background:#d8f16a;color:#192b20;padding:80px 0}.contact h2{font-size:clamp(40px,6vw,72px);letter-spacing:-.06em;line-height:1;margin:14px 0 25px}.contact .eyebrow{color:#526821}.contact .btn{background:#192b20;color:#d8f16a!important}.contact p{font-size:18px;line-height:1.7;max-width:650px}footer{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;padding:28px 24px;color:#b3c6ba;font-size:13px}:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #d8f16a;outline-offset:4px}@media(max-width:700px){.hero{min-height:560px}.hero:after{background:linear-gradient(#101b1d7a,#101b1df2)}.section{padding:60px 0}.gallery{grid-template-columns:1fr}.gallery a:first-child{grid-column:span 1}.gallery a:first-child img{aspect-ratio:4/3}}
</style></head>
<body><header class="wrap top"><a class="brand" href="/">Marc Sherwood<b>.</b></a><nav class="nav" aria-label="Suzanne navigation"><a href="#story">The story</a><a href="#photos">Photos</a><a href="/rm250/">RM250</a><a href="#contact">Inquire</a></nav></header><main>
<section class="hero"><img src="/assets/rm125/finished-side.jpg" alt="Suzanne, the yellow 2007 Suzuki RM125 with red-and-black seat" fetchpriority="high"/><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">2007 Suzuki RM125 · Frame-up rebuild</div><h1>Meet<br/>Suzanne<span style="color:#d8f16a">.</span></h1><p>A little two-stroke Suzuki with a name, a history and a second chapter.</p><a class="btn" href="#photos">See the transformation ↓</a></div></section>
<section class="section" id="story"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">01 / The story</div><h2>More than a fresh set of plastics.</h2><div class="copy"><p>Suzanne is my <strong>2007 Suzuki RM125</strong>. Rather than simply cleaning her up, I took on a <strong>frame-up rebuild</strong> — the kind of project where the motorcycle comes apart and goes back together one piece at a time.</p><p>The project photos follow the transformation from the earlier yellow-and-white bike to the rebuilt motocrosser, including the stripped frame, components, engine work, reassembly and finished result.</p><p>She is the little sister of my <a href="/rm250/" style="color:#d8f16a">2008 Suzuki RM250</a>. Both have their own stories and their own pages. Suzanne might also be available to go to a new home along with the 250.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section alt" id="photos"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">02 / The transformation</div><h2>Before, during and after.</h2><p class="copy">These are photos of the actual bike, not catalogue images. Open a photo to see it larger.</p><div class="gallery">{photos.map(photo=><a href={photo.src} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img src={photo.src} alt={photo.alt} loading="lazy"/><span>{photo.caption} ↗</span></a>)}</div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="sister"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">03 / Big sister</div><h2>Two Suzukis. Two stories.</h2><p class="copy">The 2008 RM250 is a different bike, with race-oriented equipment, a Magura hydraulic clutch, Too-Trick Racing suspension and a Pro Circuit exhaust. If a two-stroke pair is your idea of a good garage, take a look.</p><a class="btn" href="/rm250/">Explore the RM250 ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="contact" id="contact"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">04 / Contact</div><h2>Ask about Suzanne.</h2><p>Interested in the rebuild story or in giving her a new home? I'm in Richmond, British Columbia. Get in touch to talk about Suzanne or both Suzukis together.</p><a class="btn" href="mailto:marcsherwood@gmail.com?subject=Suzanne%20-%202007%20RM125%20Inquiry">Email about Suzanne ↗</a></div></section>
</main><footer class="wrap"><span>© Marc Sherwood · Richmond, BC</span><a href="/">Back to marcsherwood.com</a></footer></body></html>